1.2. "You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights granted under this License.

1.3. "Software" means source code, object code, executable files, libraries, scripts, configuration files, and other software materials expressly distributed under this License.

1.4. "Documentation" means manuals, technical specifications, reference materials, tutorials, explanatory texts, diagrams, and other documentation expressly distributed under this License.

1.5. "Licensed Material" means Software, Documentation, or both, as identified by a license notice accompanying the relevant material.

1.6. "Source Form" means the form of a work preferred for making modifications, including source code, editable document files, configuration files, and editable diagram files.

1.7. "Object Form" means a form resulting from compilation, conversion, rendering, or another transformation, including executable binaries, rendered documents, and exported diagrams.

1.8. "Modified Material" means Licensed Material that has been changed, adapted, translated, annotated, rearranged, or otherwise modified.

1.9. "Distribution" means providing, transferring, publishing, or otherwise making a copy of Licensed Material available to another party.

1.10. "Official Material" means material expressly identified by the Licensor or the relevant project maintainer as an official release or publication.

1.11. "Third-Party Material" means any material whose rights are held by someone other than the Licensor and that is not independently licensed under this License by its rights holder.

